From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Silicon Bakery (t6020 port)" <noreply@localhost>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:42:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] 4:2:2, 4:4:4 and 4:0:0 input: H.264 High 4:2:2/4:4:4, HEVC
 RExt

With enc_chroma_formats=1 (default 0) OUTPUT also offers NV16, NV24 and
GREY. The chroma format is coded as given: H.264 moves to High 4:2:2
(122), High 4:4:4 Predictive (244) or High (4:0:0); HEVC to Format range
extensions (profile 4, Main 4:2:2 10 / Main 4:4:4 (10) / Monochrome
(10)). 10-bit 4:2:2/4:4:4 input has no V4L2 fourcc in 7.2.14 (no
P210/P410); NV16/NV24 with HEVC_PROFILE MAIN_10 codes 10-bit from 8-bit.

Wire fields:
- SPS chroma_format_idc: H.264 0x105D8 (SPS+0x28; [FW] the AVC IEP takes
  the pipe's chroma format and source code 0x12/0x14/0x16 from it),
  HEVC SPS+0x23C (with 0xFEB4 = 16, "input as the SPS" [FW] 0x82e40).
- SPS cropping / conformance window in SubWidthC/SubHeightC units.
- HEVC PTL: profile_idc 4, compat[4] only, and the nine RExt constraint
  flags at PTL+0x30..+0x38 [FW HEVC_PTL::ptl_parameters 0x1a1ec], set
  per H.265 Table A.2.
- PICMGMT in_chroma_stride (+0x8D8) = 2 x stride for NV24 [FW
  CDMAController::ConfigPipeRdDMA 0x3bab8 reads it as given].
Buffer sizes [KEXT13.5]:
- recon: AVE_CalcBufSizeOfRecon (0xfffffe0008eb177c), DevType > 8 arm:
  chroma columns from w/2 (4:2:0, 4:2:2) or w (4:4:4), rows from h/2
  (4:2:0) or h, no chroma planes for 4:0:0;
- coded: AVE_CalcBufSizeOfCodedData (0xfffffe0008eb1438): 4:2:2 x1.5
  up to 921600 px else x1.2, 4:4:4 x1.6 else x1.3;
- HEVC entropy: AVE_CalcBufSizeOfEntropyCoding (0xfffffe0008eb22b0)
  per-CTB 2304 / 3072 / 4608 / 1536 for 4:2:0 / 4:2:2 / 4:4:4 / 4:0:0.
LowResRef, colocated and SrcNeighbor sizes do not depend on chroma on
DevType 16. [LIVE] macOS 27.2 encodes all of these on this Mac. B frames
are refused for H.264 122/244 (untested). Untested on hardware.
